{% comment -%}
A module's learner page, modules/<name>.md, written from the module catalog (decision 411; the spec is
Documentation/v0.2/module-reference-generation.md). Each fact comes from its one home: the module's and each action's
description; the module's guide (module.guide.md) and each action's guide (<action>.guide.md, after its Returns line),
learner prose the builder never reads; never the notes, which are the builder's; the steps of the action's examples;
each property's type, whether it is required and its default, from its handler; how a step says it and what it
changes, from the action's notes (action.Note), passed through as written. What the action returns is its notes'
Returns line, else its type. Actions come in catalog order, properties in their handler's order.
Needs: module (one element of %!app.module.list%).
{%- endcomment -%}
